From 6e0670ea6a8aee365c44499c61f50931af659d5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gf691271 <gf691271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:54:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] research: capability dump, raw type-id sweep, dict-sleep
 probe

Three opt-in, read-only helpers for the questions the second review round left open.
All three default to off and run at most once per process.

- logDeclaredCapabilities(): one CAPS line per sync listing what the watch actually
  declares (dual socket, truSleep + its newSync bits, dict sleep, hr, realtime hr, spo2,
  stress). Gadgetbridge silently falls back when a capability is missing, so "feature
  does not work" and "device never claimed it" look identical in a log.

- probeRawTypeIds() + SendRawTypeProbeRequest: ask 0x2C for type bytes that are not in the
  enumerated list (0x1A-0x40, 0x7F, 0xFF). 26 known types all answer with a full TLV and
  0x7F = 0x23281 with size 0, and 0x23281 appears nowhere upstream, so there are two
  readings: "valid type, no data" or "generic nothing to give". An impossible type byte
  separates them. addToResponse = false, so the answer never enters the download queue and
  nothing is transferred.

- tryDictSleepOnce(): request the dict-based sleep sequence (SLEEP_DETAILS_CLASS = 700013)
  even when the device does not declare support, and write the payload to files/probe/
  before parsing. sleep_data.bin has not changed since 11-13 even on worn nights; the dict
  path is a different shape of the same information and may be handed out only once.

Compiled: assembleMainlineDebug BUILD_OK. Not installed yet: the RRI capture window was
about to open, and restarting the app would have put a hole in tonight's data.
